  "worked_solution": "We can rearrange the equation to isolate the absolute value on the left side:\n\nFirst, we subtract $20$ from both sides of the equation:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-8|2x+1|+20 & =4 \\\\ -8|2x+1|+20-20 & =4-20 \\\\ -8|2x+1| & =-16\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we divide both sides of the equation by $-8:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-8|2x+1| & =-16 \\\\ \\frac{-8|2x+1|}{-8} & =\\frac{-16}{-8} \\\\ \\frac{\\cancel{-8}|2x+1|}{\\cancel{-8}} & =2 \\\\ |2x+1| & =2\\end{aligned}\n$$",
  "calculator_instructions": "",
